# A checkout here runs with core.autocrlf on, which rewrites LF to CRLF and makes
# a shell script's own interpreter line unfindable: `#!/bin/bash\r` fails with
# "cannot execute: required file not found", which reads as a missing file rather
# than a converted one. Both scripts in this directory had been converted, so
# neither would run from a fresh checkout.
#
# The same conversion is what reports files as modified while `git diff --numstat`
# shows no changed lines at all.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.R     text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf
